# Per-CVE exceptions only — see CLAUDE.md's CI-fix notes for the reasoning
# behind each entry. Never add a blanket suppression here; every line below
# must name a specific CVE with a specific, verified reason.

# CVE-2026-53571 (vite, HIGH) and CVE-2026-47429 (vitest, CRITICAL): the
# same dev-tooling chain ci.yml's `npm audit --omit=dev` already excludes
# with identical reasoning ("dev tooling... carries known advisories in
# code paths this project never runs (a dev server we don't start)").
# apps/api and apps/gateway's Dockerfiles run a full `npm ci` (not
# `--omit=dev`), because tsx/typescript ARE genuine runtime dependencies
# there (no separate tsc build step — see CLAUDE.md's Phase 14 notes), so
# vitest/vite ship into the image as a side effect, unlike npm audit which
# is scoped to skip them.
#
# Verified via GitHub's security-advisories API, not assumed: CVE-2026-
# 53571 is a `server.fs.deny` bypass requiring Vite's own dev server (`vite
# dev`) to be actively running and network-reachable; CVE-2026-47429 is an
# arbitrary-file-read requiring Vitest's UI server (`vitest --ui`) to be
# listening. Neither this codebase's Dockerfiles nor its CI ever start
# either server — tests run via `vitest run`, non-interactively, with no
# server exposed. vite here is used exclusively as vitest's internal
# transform engine.
CVE-2026-53571
CVE-2026-47429
